# Canonical production-source baseline established at 0fafdd4 and block count
# ratcheted after the include-scope audit (2026-08-12).
# Scope: Rust files below src/. Test-only Rust is reported separately.
#
# Increasing a ceiling requires a separately reviewed security rationale.
# Decreases should be committed after an audited cleanup checkpoint so the
# ratchet cannot drift back upward.
# crypt-callable-salt-contracts: three deliberately added native boundary
# blocks (crypt_ra/copy, allocation release, lazy loading/capability), no new unsafe
# functions. Review rationale and full ownership proof: docs/crypt-boundary.md.
# php-heap (2026-09-27): the PHP-tailored global allocator (src/heap) adds
# 127 blocks and 40 unsafe functions: page carving over one reserved mapping,
# a page-header array, per-page intrusive free lists, the lock-free
# remote-free/ownership protocol, version-tagged page and large-block stacks
# (ABA-safe), OS-page-aligned reclaim, a local-exec TLS heap block, the
# x86-64 asm fast-path leaves and their entry points, the GlobalAlloc
# contract and the php-heap-debug checks (free-slot bitmap, poison).
# Invariants and ownership proof: docs/php-heap-design.md. The user waived the
# ceiling for this work.
# Rust-only heap completion (2026-09-28): remove the native TLS assembly,
# optional naked fast paths and their wrappers: eight blocks and eight unsafe
# functions removed. The TLS-destructor regression test adds one test-only
# block under src/. The existing private Rust TLS getter is used everywhere;
# its references are consumed only by this thread's synchronous heap entries.
# Proof and verification: docs/performance-php-heap-finish.md.
# Borrowed release-tree observation: one local Value-bit copy under a live
# root and a callback-free, read-only graph walk. Opaque visitor snapshots and
# their descendants retain ownership. Proof and gates: performance-phpstan-parity.
# Pending-only GC boundary: one extraction block for the same existing live
# frame accesses. No new raw-pointer operation or unsafe function; the origin
# uses safe NonNull::from. Integrator safety review and exact boundary gates:
# docs/performance-phpstan-parity.md, pending-only collection state.
RPHP_UNSAFE_BASELINE_BLOCKS=1749
RPHP_UNSAFE_BASELINE_FUNCTIONS=321
RPHP_UNSAFE_BASELINE_SAFETY_COMMENTS=58
RPHP_UNSAFE_BASELINE_SAFETY_SECTIONS=0
